{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Let not [another] praise you</b> — two joined words. The meaning: Do not boast about an act of righteousness on account of tomorrow's day, so that you say: Tomorrow I will do it." "<b>Yeled</b> — like \"the generations of Jacob\" (Genesis 37:2), the sense of occurrences; and so this is as though the occurrence were born, meaning that you do not know what the day's occurrences will bring you, nor can you do it tomorrow, in the sense of \"if not now, when.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:58.315566819Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}